@startuml
actor Author
participant Browser
participant "Laravel Router" as Router
participant "Auth/Verified Middleware" as Middleware
participant "StorePostRequest" as Request
participant PostController
participant "Filesystem Disk" as Disk
database Database

Author -> Browser: Enter title/content and choose visibility
Browser -> Router: POST post.store
Router -> Middleware: Check auth and email verification
Middleware --> Router: Allow request
Router -> Request: Validate request fields
Request --> PostController: Validated data
PostController -> PostController: Reject empty published content
opt Image is present
  PostController -> Disk: Store image under uploads/posts
  Disk --> PostController: Stored path
end
PostController -> PostController: Generate unique title slug
PostController -> Database: Insert Post
Database --> PostController: Created record
PostController --> Browser: Redirect to dashboard with status
note over PostController,Database
HTML sanitization and robust orphan-file cleanup
are not established in the current implementation.
end note
@enduml
